from pathlib import Path
import json,html
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];rows=json.loads((r/'reference/plan-measurements.json').read_text());target=r/'app/public/measurements';target.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
body=''.join(f'<tr><td>{html.escape(d["id"].replace("-"," "))}</td><td>{d["width_m"]:.2f} m</td><td>±{d["uncertainty_m"]*100:.0f} cm</td><td>{d["opening_pixels"][0]}–{d["opening_pixels"][1]}</td><td>{d["wall_pixels"][0]}–{d["wall_pixels"][1]} / {d["label_m"]:.2f} m</td></tr>' for d in rows)
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><link rel="icon" href="data:,"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Danish Villa — dimension evidence</title><style>body{margin:40px auto;padding:0 22px;max-width:1040px;background:#f8f7f0;color:#253b35;font:16px/1.6 system-ui}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia}a{color:#845034}img{max-width:100%;width:700px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #d6d8cd;padding:12px}.scroll{overflow:auto}.note{background:#eeeee3;padding:20px;border-left:4px solid #8a6442}</style><a href="../">← Back to the house</a><h1>Dimensions, with their evidence.</h1><p>Danish Villa · main plan IMG_9962 · refinement 2</p><div class="note">These are image-derived dimensions, not a survey. The ranges below are conservative working estimates of uncertainty, not statistical confidence intervals. Photo perspectives and this indicative plan cannot establish millimetre accuracy.</div><h2>The entrance step</h2><p>The earlier model applied the entrance's 1.87 m label to its whole width. The supplied plan shows a step beside the guest WC. Applying 1.87 m to the wider end allows the main kitchen, office and northern room widths to close without changing the labelled bedrooms.</p><p><strong>7.57 kitchen + 0.12 partition + 3.47 office = 11.16 m.</strong><br>North: 2.40 utility + 0.12 partition + 2.28 bathroom + 0.12 partition + <strong>1.66 upper hall</strong> + 0.12 partition + 4.46 bedroom = 11.16 m.</p><p>The difference 1.87 − 1.66 = <strong>0.21 m</strong> is the inferred step depth. The existence of the step is plan-backed; its exact depth and the assumed 0.12 m walls require on-site confirmation. The guest WC's lower footprint follows this stepped boundary.</p><h2>Opening measurements</h2><p>Each opening is scaled against its own clear wall: <em>opening pixel span ÷ wall pixel span × room length</em>. Local scaling avoids treating the entire drawing as uniformly scaled. Widths are rounded to centimetres; frame and reveal edges remain ambiguous by several pixels. Vertical heights still come from photo proportions.</p><p>Example: living west window = (786 − 722) ÷ (833 − 558) × 5.00 = <strong>1.16 m</strong>, replacing the earlier 1.81 m estimate. The photo confirms a single window beside the garden door, with a horizontal division. The front-door calculation uses the inferred 1.66 m upper-hall width rather than a printed dimension.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Opening</th><th>Width</th><th>Working uncertainty</th><th>Opening pixels</th><th>Wall pixels / reference length</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+body+'''</tbody></table></div><h2>Supplied main plan</h2><img src="../photos/IMG_9962.webp" alt="Supplied main floor plan including room labels and stepped entrance wall"><h2>What still needs measurement</h2><p>Door hinge positions, exact cabinet module widths/depths, window heights and sill levels, external wall thickness and pitched ceiling heights remain estimates. The living-room H:267 annotation is retained as 2.67 m at the modeled ridge, but its intended datum is unclear. Cabinet forms and positions were checked against multiple photographs; the material appearance is illustrative.</p><p>The first useful checks are the two entrance widths, the WC return depth, one ceiling/eave height, and the kitchen counter lengths. These would constrain the remaining uncertainty more effectively than further visual guesses.</p></html>'''
# Actual photo filename uses the manifest's original stem conventions.
manifest=json.loads((r/'app/public/photos/manifest.json').read_text());plan=next(p['web'] for p in manifest if p['filename']=='IMG_9962.JPG');page=page.replace('IMG_9962.webp',plan)
(target/'index.html').write_text(page)
